# Mediyyu — build-time configuration
#
# Copy this file to ".env" (same folder) and fill in your own credentials:
#
#   cp .env.example .env
#
# ".env" is gitignored, so it never leaves your machine.
#
# No credentials are kept in the source, so in a fresh checkout the three
# features below are simply off until you supply your own. Register your own
# applications rather than reusing someone else's: the requests then count
# against your quotas, and nobody else's key gets rate-limited by your build.
#
# Everything here is optional and independent. Mediyyu plays music, reads and
# writes tags, shows lyrics and finds covers on MusicBrainz without any of it.
#
# Real environment variables always win over this file, and a .env next to the
# executable wins over one packaged inside the app.


# ── Discogs ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# A second source for covers, and for the "fill from discogs / musicbrainz"
# button in the properties dialog. Register an application to get a consumer
# key and secret:
#   https://www.discogs.com/settings/developers
# Both halves are needed. Without them, only MusicBrainz answers.
MEDIYYU_DISCOGS_KEY=
MEDIYYU_DISCOGS_SECRET=


# ── Last.fm ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Scrobbling, and the "play something similar" autoplay. Create an API account
# to get an API key and shared secret:
#   https://www.last.fm/api/account/create
# Both halves are needed. Without them, connecting an account reports that this
# build has no key.
MEDIYYU_LASTFM_KEY=
MEDIYYU_LASTFM_SECRET=


# ── Discord rich presence ───────────────────────────────────────────────────
# The application whose name and artwork appear on your Discord profile while
# a track plays. Create one at:
#   https://discord.com/developers/applications
# then copy its Application ID here. Upload your artwork under
# Rich Presence > Art Assets and name an image to match the "image key"
# setting in Mediyyu. Without this, rich presence stays off.
MEDIYYU_DISCORD_CLIENT_ID=


# ── MusicBrainz, lrclib, NetEase ────────────────────────────────────────────
# No key needed. MusicBrainz asks that applications identify themselves, which
# Mediyyu already does with its own name, version and repository URL.
